Carafe bench: samplers from a heap indexed by a constant, and samplers that force unnormalized
coordinates. DXVK 3.x indexes a sampler heap with push data; NAK builds the bindless handle as
(c[tex] & 0xfffff) | (ldc c[heap][umin(bfe(c0[push],0,16),0x7ff) << 2] & 0xfff00000). Eden took the push
data cbuf as the sampler and the mask 0xfff00000 as a shift of 20, so it read a wrong TSC entry. The texture
pass now tracks this indirect form, the descriptor keeps the heap's cbuf, offset, bit field, clamp and
shift, and the pipelines read the index at draw time to find the sampler handle. A TSC with
FLOAT_COORD_NORMALIZATION = FORCE_UNNORMALIZED (NVK sets it for unnormalized samplers, DXVK's HUD font
uses one) now makes the shader sample with unnormalized coordinates: ReadTextureType reports Color2DRect
for such a sampler and the sample patch for rectangle textures runs on implicit and explicit LOD samples.
Before, the HUD text sampled the font with pixel coordinates as if normalized and drew nothing.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.
